{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/35683-inspirations-for-lunar-spirit-shapes","id":35683,"title":"Inspirations for Lunar Spirit Shapes?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-12-23T11:15:49-08:00","id":35683,"title":"Inspirations for Lunar Spirit Shapes?","content":"Hello all, I love Lunars, and their various and sundry shape-shifting and protean abilities. However, I am terrible at thinking up thematic spirit shapes. Thus, I turn to you; what sort of inspirations do you turn to for Lunar spirit shapes? Also, what sort of memorable and/or unusual spirit shapes have you used?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T11:43:57-08:00","id":35702,"title":"","content":"I tend to start with a desired visual and then back-engineer to the appropriate beasty.<br /> <br /> Of the four Lunar concepts I've had myself, we have a road-runner, an owl, an aurochs, a <i>whale</i>, and a character whose totem hasn't been assigned yet. From NPCs and other players, I've also seen bat, cat, wolverine, bear, SPAAAAAACE PHOENIX in Heaven's Reach, and 'horrific multi-headed lamprey-mouthed hydra snake', because with Ancient Pulp Logic that is totally a legitimate 'natural' species.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T12:22:17-08:00","id":35721,"title":"","content":"In games, I've seen wolf, gryphon, tyrant lizard, horse, lizard, and hawk. I've only played one Lunar, and his totem animal was a giant albatross.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T12:25:11-08:00","id":35722,"title":"","content":"David Attenborough documentaries.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://jaxushomebrew.blogspot.ie/2016/06/introduction-site-map-and-catalogue.html\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew blog</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1291-mr-jaxus","name":"Mr.Jaxus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1291_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T12:54:54-08:00","id":35744,"title":"","content":"Personally, I favor symbolism and mythic resonance of an animal before anything else.* The physical traits are cool, too, but the associations have always been my favorite part, whether playing them straight or playing against type. I'd suggest looking up animal symbolism or reading a lot of animal fables/stories. Human cultures have created no shortage of both. Whether starting with a human character and then finding an appropriate animal, or starting with an animal and then working back to the sort of character to receive such a shape, I think it works quite well.<br /> <br /> I haven't actually made many Lunar characters myself. Still, I've had a few concepts bouncing around. A hawk-totem former prince archer raining death from on high with a very severe temperment. A donkey-totem vagabond Changing or No Moon with a cheerful tendency to play the fool, both for finding it fun in its own right and for duping others into severely underestimating him. A mongoose-totem wandering teacher to the destitute, both in the martial arts and anything else, really. I rather liked the anima idea for the last, the giant stylistic mongoose centered the Lunar, while the rest of his banner created great serpents out of negative space around nearby foes, the anima imagery playing out representative of the actual battle.<br /> <br /> * Tangent: I'm really hopeful that this winds up playing more of a role in EX3's execution; in 2e spirit shapes, physical traits were the only ones backed up mechanically. I'd be thrilled if animals even without much direct utility and/or with outclassed stats, but flush with symbolic meaning, still felt mechanically useful as a spirit shape to a Lunar. The idea hatewheel contemplated about choice of spirit shape letting one get easier access to and/or shift around Charm trees sounded like it could really work with that. I'd find it very cool if you could let mechanics back you up when selecting between, say, a raven, a dove, a mockingbird, and a sparrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T12:58:06-08:00","id":35748,"title":"","content":"I have an idea for a hyena Lunar. Her Tell is the laugh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T13:22:52-08:00","id":35769,"title":"","content":"So how does mythic resonance work if your spirit shape is a non-avian dinosaur? They kind of died out before humans in real life saw them. Would you just go with dragon legends, what with fossils often being likened to dragon bones?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T14:26:58-08:00","id":35808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/35683-inspirations-for-lunar-spirit-shapes?p=35769#post35769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So how does mythic resonance work if your spirit shape is a non-avian dinosaur? They kind of died out before humans in real life saw them. Would you just go with dragon legends, what with fossils often being likened to dragon bones?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say playing off notions of dragons could indeed provide some cool stuff, if one wanted to go that way. But by and large, the approach of symbolism and mythic resonance isn't an especially helpful one for prehistoric creatures, or creatures that were otherwise unknown to or undescribed by peoples of old (a lotta cool stuff deep below the ocean, for instance). This is a weakness inherent to the method that doesn't bother me personally because of my tastes: I really enjoy reading and learning more about symbolism and folklore. Those are just the areas in which I'd want to make sure I had a happy body of material to play with for a Lunar's spirit shape. I am completely okay that this means I miss out on some very cool creatures because they just don't have any myths or folklore about them. One who isn't okay with that is probably not going to find my method very satisfying, or will want to use it as just one method out of several.<br /> <br /> Naturally, one should always feel free to create the context oneself where it's lacking, or even where it isn't. There's little in the way of legends, symbolism and folklore specific to non-avian dinosaurs in our world, but the cultures of Creation would surely have developed plenty. It doesn't need to be exhaustive, but coming up with some things to work with is an entirely reasonable option.<br /> <br /> To clarify, I'm not suggesting mythic resonance be the only factor in a spirit shape. I just personally find it really cool and want it as an option.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T14:28:35-08:00","id":35809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Valles</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/35683-inspirations-for-lunar-spirit-shapes?p=35702#post35702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to start with a desired visual and then back-engineer to the appropriate beasty.<br /> <br /> Of the four Lunar concepts I've had myself, we have a road-runner, an owl, an aurochs, a <i>whale</i>, and a character whose totem hasn't been assigned yet. From NPCs and other players, I've also seen bat, cat, wolverine, bear, SPAAAAAACE PHOENIX in Heaven's Reach, and 'horrific multi-headed lamprey-mouthed hydra snake', because with Ancient Pulp Logic that is totally a legitimate 'natural' species.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yo dawg, he's a STAAAAAAR HAWK.<br /> <br /> Ultimately the spirit totem is only as important as the feels it can express. It should capture an aspect of the character that deserves emphasis, because mechanically they don't matter too much. Yes, your spirit totem determines what kinds of mutations you can take for your war form, but you can get nice things with virtually any kind of totem spirit.<br /> <br /> Other than that, just pick something you find cool. If you're stumped, try arkive.org and just browse until you find something intriguing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T15:01:52-08:00","id":35826,"title":"","content":"For my own part, I just use common stereotypes about the animal in question as a starting-off point: If they're a sheep they're a follower, etc. After that, I look around at folktales, and so forth.<br /> <br /> As for the totems I've used--I've had a snake totem, an octopus totem, and a sheep totem. Also vague plans of a horned toad totem and horse totem. I'd be happy to tell you about any of them. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/781-chained-divinity","name":"Chained Divinity","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar781_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T15:31:06-08:00","id":35844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So how does mythic resonance work if your spirit shape is a non-avian dinosaur? They kind of died out before humans in real life saw them. Would you just go with dragon legends, what with fossils often being likened to dragon bones?</div> </div> </div> </div> I'd say that if people saw T-Rexes, they'd attribute much the same resonance to them as, say, tigers crossed with elephants.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T18:01:31-08:00","id":35962,"title":"","content":"My lunar's Spirit form is a Utah Raptor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T19:39:06-08:00","id":36023,"title":"","content":"My favorite Spirit Animal I actually kind of had to make up.<br /> <br /> I was playing a No Moon in the West, so I needed to come up with a water animal that symbolized cunning. My options were fairly limited (turtle, dolphin, giant squid--which the darn full moon had already taken) so I instead turned to myth.<br /> <br /> Catfish.<br /> <br /> In Japan there are several myths about Catfish, on involves a fish that lives under the island...one that's so damn big it makes all the earthquakes, another involves a Catfish swallowing the MOON (lunar senses tingling) and only by catching the fish were they able to return the moon to the sky. And of course my personal favorite, if a carp (catfish relative) swims up a waterfall it turns in to a dragon.<br /> <br /> Add the standard american fish stories (the one that got away, the king of the pond) and solarize it.(&quot;fishing is boring! Let's make a fish so awesome it makes the sport of fishing interesting again!&quot;). I named it the &quot;Rainbow Coy&quot; and said my pre-exaltation lunar saw one &quot;eat the moon&quot; one calibration and resolved to catch it. It took him all of calibration but he did finally catch that fish...and caught a Luna at the same time.<br /> <br /> I named him Garadoc the Cunning (a pun on &quot;Gyarados&quot;--the dragon said carp turn into), and gave him the worst tell in the world...his skin sparkles like fish scales. Too bad that game didn't last.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>I'M SORRY, I CAN'T HEAR YOU OVER THE SOUND OF HOW MANY MALFEAS CHARMS I HAVE!!!</b><i>~King Crazy Genius</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/345-kandagger","name":"Kandagger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar345_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"30"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T19:58:38-08:00","id":36036,"title":"","content":"Wow my Raptor guy has a full set of fangs and can only eat meat...I think you had a worse tell than I did.<br /> Then again our Snake Lunar has a forked tounge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T21:05:18-08:00","id":36073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kandagger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/35683-inspirations-for-lunar-spirit-shapes?p=36023#post36023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My favorite Spirit Animal I actually kind of had to make up.<br /> <br /> I was playing a No Moon in the West, so I needed to come up with a water animal that symbolized cunning. My options were fairly limited (turtle, dolphin, giant squid--which the darn full moon had already taken) so I instead turned to myth.<br /> <br /> Catfish.<br /> <br /> In Japan there are several myths about Catfish, on involves a fish that lives under the island...one that's so damn big it makes all the earthquakes, another involves a Catfish swallowing the MOON (lunar senses tingling) and only by catching the fish were they able to return the moon to the sky. And of course my personal favorite, if a carp (catfish relative) swims up a waterfall it turns in to a dragon.<br /> <br /> Add the standard american fish stories (the one that got away, the king of the pond) and solarize it.(&quot;fishing is boring! Let's make a fish so awesome it makes the sport of fishing interesting again!&quot;). I named it the &quot;Rainbow Coy&quot; and said my pre-exaltation lunar saw one &quot;eat the moon&quot; one calibration and resolved to catch it. It took him all of calibration but he did finally catch that fish...and caught a Luna at the same time.<br /> <br /> I named him Garadoc the Cunning (a pun on &quot;Gyarados&quot;--the dragon said carp turn into), and gave him the worst tell in the world...his skin sparkles like fish scales. Too bad that game didn't last.</div> </div> </div> </div>In what will now be considered forever irony, said &quot;starhawk&quot; is played by me and is based upon the mythology of the Kun and Peng. It fits the character, who values his personal freedom highly and is &quot;a secret philosopher.&quot; His totemic anima is a giant silver-and-gray shadow of a wing permeating the area that silver droplets leap out of or fall into (not really specified because magic) in time with the beating of his heart.<br /> <br /> This is Heaven's Reach, however, so this giant raptor flies between planets in a system of hellworlds used to train Imperial special forces that my character resided on for a decade after being selected for his shard. He saw the birds and immediately recognized kindred spirits, fighting gravity and rationality to be free. I think he has used his spirit form once in the entire game.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaplessWithDice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/35683-inspirations-for-lunar-spirit-shapes?p=36036#post36036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow my Raptor guy has a full set of fangs and can only eat meat...I think you had a worse tell than I did.<br /> Then again our Snake Lunar has a forked tounge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tells in general are awful when they are used to punish a player. They're not even a good mechanic when used with a Lunar NPC.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T21:10:10-08:00","id":36078,"title":"","content":"Well they give you away to anyone looking at you.<br /> And a guy who can only eat raw meat, and has the teeth of a dinosaur kinda stands out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T21:23:57-08:00","id":36084,"title":"","content":"Between the games I'm playing in/running right now, there are, as either PCs or actively-involved NPCs: two tigers (a Siberian Full-Moon and a Sumatran No-Moon), a mimic octopus, a shield mantis, a hummingbird, a spider of indeterminate species, a coyote, and a dragonfly.<br /> <br /> Wow, in hindsight that's a lot of invertebrates.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dayen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/35683-inspirations-for-lunar-spirit-shapes?p=36073#post36073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tells in general are awful when they are used to punish a player. They're not even a good mechanic when used with a Lunar NPC.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like many, many, <i>many</i> things in the gameline, they're a neat idea with shitty execution. I wrote a rules hack so they're an actual asset and not just a forced botch on disguises, and I suspect I am not alone in this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1024-thesaurasaurus","name":"Thesaurasaurus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-23T22:08:27-08:00","id":36126,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thesaurasaurus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/35683-inspirations-for-lunar-spirit-shapes?p=36084#post36084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like many, many, <i>many</i> things in the gameline, they're a neat idea with shitty execution. I wrote a rules hack so they're an actual asset and not just a forced botch on disguises, and I suspect I am not alone in this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like most bad mechanics, it tends to get ignored during actual play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/889-dayen","name":"Dayen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"330"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-24T04:27:04-08:00","id":36293,"title":"","content":"My Lunar - the albatross-totem - had the Tell of a voice that boomed like ocean waves. Mostly because I liked the old-school Tells better and didn't want him to have feathers or some crap (besides, the feathers stuff is already Lillith's Tell).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T01:31:26-08:00","id":37758,"title":"","content":"One character I hope to one day play is a No Moon Lunar whose totem is a Termite King. He'll have a romantic fixation on the Queen - his Solar bond-mate (who may or may not be a woman, whatever would fit better) - and be into mega-scale engineering, big time. He'll have tons of territory and mass combat charms, breed millions of fanatically loyal Ata- and San-Insects and beastmen, and be a genuinely good if somewhat creepy guy dedicated to his people and the world.<br /> <br /> His hat will be geomancy, specifically a slowly expanding network of Manses, possibly located in a stabilised Waypoint in the Wyld, alternatively an Elsewhere-den, possibly both and neither for maximal Schroedinger points.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Aretii: &quot;As one of the players described it, 'After initiation, it was actually a relief seeing who had eyepatches or bandaged hands - you know what <i>they</i> sacrificed, instead of wondering what bits people cut out of their own souls to gain power.'&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/578-lord-sia","name":"Lord Sia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T02:17:03-08:00","id":37770,"title":"","content":"My Lunar:<br /> <br /> Spirit Shape<br /> Nibiru, Artisan of the Vital Essence - Nibiru appears as a dark brooding storm striking out with flashes of genius. Its arms winding out as the currents of the sea and air \u2013 she ejects ink in masterful swirls that slowly take one of a thousand shapes, each coming to life.<br /> <br /> It's based on a squid and injected with spirituality - going beyond an animal lacking long term memory and more interested in eating than anything else. I think serious spin needs to be put on any animal to become a spiritual totem. Simply having a totem of wolf or hawk or monkey is boring for something that so speaks for the splat and what it means to be a Lunar. Becoming a Lunar means discovering a driving force and soul within that you never knew about - but was always there. The blessing of Luna simply awoke it and made it a tangible force. Cats mean a dozen things to a dozen cultures - the totem should take upon itself features and aspects of your personal mythos. <br /> <br /> ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> If your totem is a Walrus and you believe <i>walruses </i>are dogged beasts with endless fonts of strength then let that show in your totem. It is not simply a Walrus. Your totem is Himanada, He that Grinds the World - Himanada appears as a hulk of translucent grey stone that glows with inner fire - fire that constantly melts the rime that seeks to consume his body in the icy cold seas of time. His hunger is unending and insatiable as he gorges himself upon the old to fuel the heartfires that stave off cold sterile certainty. <br /> <br /> Himanada could be represented by any aggressive innovator. Tearing down old tired governments for new ones up to date with the times, destroying hide-bound technologies for a better way, anything that destroys misplaced tradition for modernization and progress.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","name":"The Despot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T08:18:58-08:00","id":37867,"title":"","content":"Despot, I love the way you think. Let's see...<br /> <br /> Tchiss Lk'Kx, Who Is The Tower And The Well, the Termite King. His real body is tall and slender, skin pale - almost translucent - with only a diaphanous gown oddly reminiscent of wings. His voice is soft yet persuasive, sometimes seeming to echo as if a whispering choir of thousands repeated his words. When his power unfolds, a white spire is silhouetted against a dark moon, and his body disappears into the shadowy depths of the bottomless well beneath that tower. And there is truth in this, for even from the deepest of the hidden chamber in his palatial city-manse, he still knows everything that occurs in his realm as though he were present.<br /> <br /> The Termite King will never fight an open battle if he has a choice; he prefers diplomacy to war, and if he must fight, he does so defensively - drawing his enemies into elaborate traps, forcing them to exhaust themselves against impregnable defences, and generally wearing them down without actually fighting them. He never fights in person, preferring to direct his troops from afar, supporting them with powerful magic and technology, well aware that he is a skilled combatant - for a mortal. By Exalted standards, he is hopeless.<br /> <br /> He is, above all, a dreamer, a builder and a thinker; a loyal Sun King Seneschal and a member of the Crossroads Society, he longs for the day when he will be re-united with his bond-mate. Ironically, the return of the Solars has actually served to ground him. Where before, his eventual reunion was more of a fanciful dream of regaining glories long lost, it is now a inevitable fact. A fact tainted by the rumours of some Solars having come back <i>wrong</i>, not to mention the sheer odds against his mate being what he dreamt she would be - in fact, it is a fifty-fifty chance of <i>she</i> being a <i>he.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Aretii: &quot;As one of the players described it, 'After initiation, it was actually a relief seeing who had eyepatches or bandaged hands - you know what <i>they</i> sacrificed, instead of wondering what bits people cut out of their own souls to gain power.'&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/578-lord-sia","name":"Lord Sia","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"240"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T09:11:06-08:00","id":37888,"title":"","content":"I'm partial to <i>bat</i>, myself. Plenty of subspecies and a great deal of iconic features for Tells: scalloped ears, clawed feet, patagium, sightless eyes*, fangs. It's a goddamn cornucopia of possibilities! <br /> <br /> But I love, with a great deal of force, unusual Tells. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\">Isator Levi</a>'s hyena laugh is <i>way</i> fantastic. I played a <i>tiger</i>-totem Lunar with his many scars rearranged into lateral stripes. The only Lunar NPC I can remember meeting on good terms, in all my years of <i>Exalted, </i>had a <i>wolf eel</i>-totem that gave her a powerful, <i>Baron Underbheit</i> jaw.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17-metrophelean","name":"Metrophelean","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar17_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T09:40:40-08:00","id":37901,"title":"","content":"I find that easy lunar character/animal totem 'generator' is to look at the sidereal astrology charts...<br /> <br /> They have many animals and whatnots in their astrology lists<br /> <br /> Like, a seagull totem'd lunar. Can be from any direction. Prankster, surprisingly good at 'appearing busy' and doing aerial bombardments and dive-bomb attacks...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T13:07:00-08:00","id":37970,"title":"","content":"Thanks Lord Sia, I've added Tchiss Lk'Kx to my list of <i>true </i>Lunars. It's sad how often spirit shapes are shallow and hollow. Picking a spirit shape because of the tell...that speaks nothing of your soul and nothing of your true self.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","name":"The Despot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T13:18:01-08:00","id":37974,"title":"","content":"My Lunars tend to coagulate around a concept, then develop an appropriate spirit shape. The boy raised as a pure, innocent sacrifice--a concept I'd picked up from a few mentions, including Fatal Frame and American Gods--became a high-compassion, high-conviction No-Moon who would heal you the best he could, but kill you as painlessly and unhesitatingly as possible if it was necessary. His spirit shape was Lamb. Another No-Moon, a Sijanese funerist with a giant hammer and a penchant for sky burial, drew upon the imagery of dog-as-psychopomp and takes the shape of a towering black mastiff. A Changing Moon raised as the Most Dangerous Game--who survived not by fighting, but by fleeing--took the spirit shape of a deer. A former Realm layabout who fell on hard times, fled his riches, and ended up shedding everything he had been to <i>live? </i>Cicada.<br /> <br /> I figure out what I want out of a character before I latch onto a spirit shape. Usually I find one feeds the other pretty nicely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/561-mockery","name":"Mockery","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar561_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"876"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T13:31:29-08:00","id":37982,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Despot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/35683-inspirations-for-lunar-spirit-shapes?p=37770#post37770\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My Lunar:<br /> <br /> Spirit Shape<br /> Nibiru, Artisan of the Vital Essence - Nibiru appears as a dark brooding storm striking out with flashes of genius. Its arms winding out as the currents of the sea and air \u2013 she ejects ink in masterful swirls that slowly take one of a thousand shapes, each coming to life.<br /> <br /> It's based on a squid and injected with spirituality - going beyond an animal lacking long term memory and more interested in eating than anything else. I think serious spin needs to be put on any animal to become a spiritual totem. Simply having a totem of wolf or hawk or monkey is boring for something that so speaks for the splat and what it means to be a Lunar. Becoming a Lunar means discovering a driving force and soul within that you never knew about - but was always there. The blessing of Luna simply awoke it and made it a tangible force. Cats mean a dozen things to a dozen cultures - the totem should take upon itself features and aspects of your personal mythos.<br /> <br /> ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------<br /> <br /> If your totem is a Walrus and you believe <i>walruses </i>are dogged beasts with endless fonts of strength then let that show in your totem. It is not simply a Walrus. Your totem is Himanada, He that Grinds the World - Himanada appears as a hulk of translucent grey stone that glows with inner fire - fire that constantly melts the rime that seeks to consume his body in the icy cold seas of time. His hunger is unending and insatiable as he gorges himself upon the old to fuel the heartfires that stave off cold sterile certainty.<br /> <br /> Himanada could be represented by any aggressive innovator. Tearing down old tired governments for new ones up to date with the times, destroying hide-bound technologies for a better way, anything that destroys misplaced tradition for modernization and progress.</div> </div> </div> </div>To echo Lord Sia, this is a great idea, and I am stealing this process. I'm currently working on a Lunar myself, and the problem that arises is I get a great character concept, but have trouble rationalizing the mythic aspects of a tough survivor with any one animal, apart from maybe the tired cliches of wolf, fox, monkey, etc. However, this idea opens up a lot of potential, and resonates with the concept of Lunars as Bestial God-Kings, their beast aspects, just as important and mythic as their aspects as Humans.<br /> <br /> To wit, this is what I have: Edennae, the Stalker of the Throne, a marsupial lion from the Threshold, which stalks the foothills of the Scavenger lands, and exalts her nobility by finding powerful prey or competing carnivores and slaying them, decorating her lair with their bones. <br /> <br /> I am using this for a former Dynastic Scion, who, after failing to exalt as a Terrestrial, went on a number of pilgrimages to her family's Threshold Manses, got lost, and after several weeks in the wild, managed to crawl back, now with the blessing of Luna as one of Her champions. Taken in as a member of the Silver Pact, she'd be torn between her desire to revive the nobility of Humanity through the Thousand Streams River, but also torn to her old loyalty to her clan. <br /> <br /> Apart from that, I think that the conversation is great, and everyone has had great ideas and helped me quite a bit. Thanks, everyone!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T15:23:29-08:00","id":38032,"title":"","content":"Mostly I just look up animals and try to find the kinds that do something cool or weird looking in real life. Like how a cat's eyes reflect light in a dark enough room. Or how a dog's nose is the coolest part of their body.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T18:38:00-08:00","id":38102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Metrophelean</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/35683-inspirations-for-lunar-spirit-shapes?p=37888#post37888\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi\">Isator Levi</a>'s hyena laugh is <i>way</i> fantastic.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm kind of torn on whether or not it should come across as somebody with, at best, a tendency to kind of laugh inappropriately, or just amount to a kind of tic.<br /> <br /> It wasn't part of my initial supposition, but I'm kind of leaning towards the latter myself. It might even be that when she laughs from actual mirth, it sounds normal.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T19:01:24-08:00","id":38112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Despot</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">my list of <i>true </i>Lunars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh good Lord...<br /> <br /> You know, that other thread, the Lunar Picture one, that actually started me thinking &quot;is it possible that getting all caught up on the symbolic or mythic associations of the native animal form of every Lunar is just a big distraction and frustration, and that they really don't need to go much beyond a fairly neat animal&quot;.<br /> <br /> I mean, it's been pointed out that in terms of Charms, not many animal capabilities really have the mythic resonance necessary to map them, and that's all well and good for Charms, but it also kind of leaves a lot of spirit shapes out of the running if one holds them to those standards.<br /> <br /> It feels so much more straightforward to just pick an animal and go with it.<br /> <br /> That was what I was thinking before I looked back in on this thread, which reiterated to me the idea of &quot;welp, some people still want Lunars to be Silver Infernals. Specifically the Second Edition type, specifically in terms of 'let's figure out all kinds of details that make Lunars entirely incompatible with one another in a manner that would surely make a book a nightmare to write'&quot;.<br /> <br /> I don't care much for phrasing it in terms of just so many essential characteristics neither.<br /> <br /> Which leads back into my sense that attributing too much to the associations of animal shapes ultimately detracts, because I think particular varieties of Exalted are best when there's a proper coherency and consistency within their themes, and putting too much weight on the shapes either means that they lack those qualities or you wind up being limited in your pool of animals.<br /> <br /> Perhaps that's the relevance of the &quot;Lunars' association with animals is Gaia&quot; line; that, through some mythic qualities deriving from their god, there's a certain connection to Gaia there, but that's about all it is, so it manifests in assuming <i>an</i> animal form, and not much else, so they can otherwise just get on with being Lunars.<br /> <br /> This other stuff seems more suitable for the Exalted of a variety of animal gods. Or possibly suitable to fae stuff.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T22:05:39-08:00","id":38161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/35683-inspirations-for-lunar-spirit-shapes?p=38112#post38112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Perhaps that's the relevance of the &quot;Lunars' association with animals is Gaia&quot; line; that, through some mythic qualities deriving from their god, there's a certain connection to Gaia there, but that's about all it is, so it manifests in assuming <i>an</i> animal form, and not much else, so they can otherwise just get on with being Lunars.</div> </div> </div> </div>It may be that I'm misreading your intent. We actually do have indications that the EX3 spirit shape is going to be more than just an animal form that a Lunar can become. It may even have a big impact on how easily a particular Lunar can access appropriate parts of the Charmset, the last word we had (spoilered for space) :<br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is still the animal you choose to be the basis for your DBT. How much I force it into your character's appearance remains to be seen. If you don't want to be a DBT Lunar, I'd rather you think of DBT / spirit shape as the tool you relied on when your Lunar was still young, inexperienced, and less powerful, rather than ignoring it entirely. I want to help people build away from a DBT-based character through powers that work when you are in your human form and don't work when you are in DBT.<br /> <br /> Once you reach that point, it is my intention that the spirit shape, through a clever use of keywords and associations, provide you a favored discount on Charms whose Attributes you don't favor, going so far as to change the Charm's prerequisites and shift it to a logical place in your current Charm trees (if one exists). So even if you ignore your spirit shape in roleplay, its themes are there helping you by providing a framework to power up your character.<br /> <br /> I also realize that one of the reasons people search so furiously for meaning beyond DBT is because a single animal is so constraining, so I am looking at completely redoing Chimeraism so that it is an accepted state, so that players can make cool-looking hybrid monsters with lots of different traits.<br /> <br /> Note that everything I've said here is &quot;Maybe&quot; not &quot;I promise&quot; and is subject to change. This is about as far as I am willing to reach into my giant vault of future noise to show people, but I feel like the general tone of acceptance and readiness for big new ideas has reached a level where such a classified view won't confuse and upset anyone.</div> </div> </div> </div></div></div> </div> </div><br /> My hope is for mythic associations and symbolism that are actively helpful, as more of an option for Lunars than they've had. That's about all I've got. I certainly don't want it crowding out other approaches to spirit shapes that other people enjoy more.<br /> <br /> Honestly, in the talk of &quot;clever use of keywords and associations,&quot; my mind conjured up something like, &quot;Got an animal you like for your Lunar? Cool. Now, pick X of these keywords that suit your spirit shape. Go with whatever ways feel right to you: symbolism, mythic associations, scientific properties, whatever. These keywords yadda yadda yadda.&quot; In a setup vaguely like that, mythic/symbolic influences from the spirit shape could get just as much mechanical reinforcement as the player wished, just like any other considered factors.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T22:06:57-08:00","id":38162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/35683-inspirations-for-lunar-spirit-shapes?p=35748#post35748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have an idea for a hyena Lunar. Her Tell is the laugh.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have an idea for a hyena Lunar.<br /> <br /> Her Tell is not the laugh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/922-hailey-mcauliffe","name":"Hailey McAuliffe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar922_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T22:32:42-08:00","id":38167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/35683-inspirations-for-lunar-spirit-shapes?p=38112#post38112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You know, that other thread, the Lunar Picture one, that actually started me thinking &quot;is it possible that getting all caught up on the symbolic or mythic associations of the native animal form of every Lunar is just a big distraction and frustration, and that they really don't need to go much beyond a fairly neat animal&quot;.<br /> ... [cut for focus] ...<br /> It feels so much more straightforward to just pick an animal and go with it.<br /> ... [cut for focus] ...<br /> Perhaps that's the relevance of the &quot;Lunars' association with animals is Gaia&quot; line; that, through some mythic qualities deriving from their god, there's a certain connection to Gaia there, but that's about all it is, so it manifests in assuming <i>an</i> animal form, and not much else, so they can otherwise just get on with being Lunars.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem here, though, is that the Spirit Shape / Totem is repeatedly called out as being important to the character. Just as I've known people who will obsess over the tiniest details of their character's appearance, I myself would go insane trying to come up with a suitable animal for any Lunar I create. When you present a player with a permanent decision, and tell them it will serve as a defining point for their character, it is only natural that some players will want something that they feel they can grow into or connect with in a way that defies &quot;pick an animal and go with it.&quot;<br /> <br /> And that is before you get into the mechanical and story effects of the Spirit Shape. It defines your Tell, it initially defines your Warform and starting mutation set, and (perhaps most importantly for some of my players), it is the ONLY form you can permanently acquire without killing or boning.<br /> <br /> Now, if you were suggesting that 3e Lunars might benefit from a decreased emphasis on Spirit Shape, I concede that could resolve some concerns, but I feel it would also take away something that has been a major defining feature of the Lunar Exalted.<br /> <br /> Personally, after playing Alchemicals of late, I've come to appreciate their &quot;State-Designated Legend&quot; as a touchstone for guiding the character and their growth, without being locked into anything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/35683-inspirations-for-lunar-spirit-shapes?p=38112#post38112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That was what I was thinking before I looked back in on this thread, which reiterated to me the idea of &quot;welp, some people still want Lunars to be Silver Infernals. Specifically the Second Edition type, specifically in terms of 'let's figure out all kinds of details that make Lunars entirely incompatible with one another in a manner that would surely make a book a nightmare to write'&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can certainly empathize with this sentiment, but I don't think this concept of highly-symbolic Spirit Shapes MUST go the route of Infernals, Shintai, and Devil Tigers. The walrus example, for instance, could just be represented by a basic set of mutations (3e will have them as Merits, I believe), Stamina/Wits Charms, decent Willpower, and good roleplaying to bring out the personality the Spirit Shape suggests. Maybe, farther along the way, once there are no more suitable Lunar core Charms, THEN the player will work with their ST to make custom Charms, but by that point I'd imagine any splat other than Sidereals will be looking to do the same.<br /> <br /> BUT (and I stress this because I suspect it is the root cause of the Silver-Solar / Silver-Sidereal / Silver-Infernal labeling), we do not currently have a cohesive set of core Lunar Charms, and so Lunar players who desire to do anything besides combat will often turn to custom material, which will naturally borrow from other splats' mechanical styles. I expect (and hope!) 3rd Edition will alleviate this need.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />Avatar commissioned from the incomparable Melissa Uran.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/966-redford_blade","name":"Redford_Blade","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar966_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"90"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-27T23:06:42-08:00","id":38174,"title":"","content":"Totems I want at some point:<br /> <br /> Pink Underwing Moth Caterpillar<br /> Sharovipteryx (AKA Kite Lizard)<br /> Ceratogaulus (AKA Horned Gopher)<br /> Chevrotain<br /> Horned Viper<br /> Pichiciego<br /> Bilby<br /> Honey Badger","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T08:28:11-08:00","id":38294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hailey McAuliffe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/35683-inspirations-for-lunar-spirit-shapes?p=38162#post38162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I have an idea for a hyena Lunar.<br /> <br /> Her Tell is not the laugh.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is she a spotted hyena?<br /> <br /> &quot;These... are not the Tell.&quot;<br /> <br /> (walks away, then walks back) <br /> <br /> &quot;The Tell is my pseudopenis.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 12-28-2013, 11:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T10:32:40-08:00","id":38335,"title":"","content":"Its silly to talk about she-hyena penises when we are having a serious talk about Lunars. If you want to be taken seriously as a splat, to distance oneself from the feral' wipe with pine cones' view, this is exactly the thing that makes people believe that's what Lunars are. That Lunar players are contented with those themes.<br /> <br /> The Spirit Shape, from rumors of 3E, is a font of your identity. Not only informing upon parts of your behavior and mores but also establishing your paths to power. For the Lunar it is more clear and important than the 2E concept of an epic motivation, it is what you are, aspects of you soul and being given form and substance. It's deep stuff, but I understand its not a train everyone's gonna want to ride.<br /> <br /> Unlike an epic motivation to restructure the Realm or create a Northern Peace Summit as a checks and balances to the rebirth of god-kings (Solar and Lunar//Yurgan and Gerd Marrow-Eater) - someone like 'Himanada, He that Grinds the World' has a guiding principle that takes him far beyond the establishment of such a peace and even works on the micro as well as macro scale. Head into a farm village and see them hauling water up from a river, boom, your into fixing that with a well or centralized cistern. Perhaps you rail against the Silver Pact and their hide-bound rules to well...bind your hide. It provides endless stories and is a guiding light. That is something we all need in the early game, when we are not familiar with our character or their beliefs/behaviors, as well as late game when the scope of Creation, and the awesome power we wield, threatens to blur our focus and scatter our concepts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1066,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","user":"The Despot","date":". 12-28-2013, 02:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","name":"The Despot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T12:27:58-08:00","id":38377,"title":"","content":"My prior point was mostly from something I felt from the Pictures thread, and is probably still overshooting what the design will culminate in.<br /> <br /> I am okay with that, as a step in the process of figuring out what I think about certain topics; in this case, I'm still mostly concerned with reducing pressure on essential characteristics deriving from spirit shape, or vice verse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-28T14:30:48-08:00","id":38425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gaius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/35683-inspirations-for-lunar-spirit-shapes?p=35744#post35744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I favor symbolism and mythic resonance of an animal before anything else.* The physical traits are cool, too, but the associations have always been my favorite part, whether playing them straight or playing against type. I'd suggest looking up animal symbolism or reading a lot of animal fables/stories. Human cultures have created no shortage of both. Whether starting with a human character and then finding an appropriate animal, or starting with an animal and then working back to the sort of character to receive such a shape, I think it works quite well.<br /> <br /> * Tangent: I'm really hopeful that this winds up playing more of a role in EX3's execution; in 2e spirit shapes, physical traits were the only ones backed up mechanically. I'd be thrilled if animals even without much direct utility and/or with outclassed stats, but flush with symbolic meaning, still felt mechanically useful as a spirit shape to a Lunar. The idea hatewheel contemplated about choice of spirit shape letting one get easier access to and/or shift around Charm trees sounded like it could really work with that. I'd find it very cool if you could let mechanics back you up when selecting between, say, a raven, a dove, a mockingbird, and a sparrow.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are already some mechanics out there that can support these concepts to a degree, granted with limited knowledge of the new mechanics and time, these are just ideas thrown at a wall.<br /> <br /> In Changling you have effectively a Fey spirit shape, the Ice Queen and so on, which only becomes more complex as you adopt a court and noble order. These are meant to be marks upon your spirit that change you and inform upon your perspective in the world. They are all great sign posts that could be adopted for our own spirit shapes - granted using different methods that resonate better with perhaps the Werewolf line or Book of Spirits.<br /> <br /> Only because I recently checked it out and Numenera is on my mind as well - they have multi-threaded descriptors<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;I am an <i>adjective noun</i> who verbs.&quot; </div> </div> </div>Which is simple and helps to inform what kind of No Moon or Elk Totem Lunar that you are. Granted, I feel its a bit simplistic the way they carry things - running it like multi-classing. But, the base concept, still useful<br /> <br /> When one looks at legends of the Goldfish:<br /> <br /> It came from the crucian carp - selectively breed by the ruling dynasty to bring about the golden hue into the population when it was simply a mutation. Gold or Yellow being the same in Chinese culture as the royal purple in the West. The fish took on symbology of wealth, bounty and surplus and the gift of one well wishes for those same things. If China had founded the United States it is quite possible that the gold fish would be our emblem rather than the bald eagle - as the goldfish is the American Dream:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> goldfish represent the notion that it is possible for anybody to achieve whatever they want </div> </div> </div>That tells so many stories - hopes and dreams for the downtrodden of Creation.<br /> <br /> At the same time we have <i>J\u014dzu, </i>the Whopper, who is said to have eaten the moon and captured the goddess the moon represents (Yumigami). This Spirit represents hunger in any or all of its forms. A strive to consume or become more or to devour foes or to absorb nations or peoples under its cult.<br /> <br /> With the countless myths built upon animals it is really up to the player to connect to, or even build, a legend for their spirit shape and give it meaning. That there is, proposedly, a pool of mechanical benefits to connect to totems, in a free form manner, that would be a wonderful solution. Between whats been said about the use of keywords applying to Totems and the freeform nature of Exigents, I think the future is bright.<br /> <br /> The biggest issue is the investment of time and energy involved - how much does a player want to devote to establishing their totem. Currently many Lunar players wait till they grow into the character to establish a totem. Others have issues settling and may even change their totem over time. When you're going to spend hundreds, if not thousands, of hours with his character - giving your totem some though/love is well worth it. If mechanical scaffolding is in place to guide - most excellent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1066-the-despot","name":"The Despot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-12-29T14:39:20-08:00","id":38889,"title":"","content":"I suppose it all comes down to player preference for flavor details, then. In a related example, I've heard many complain about how &quot;All Daiklaives are the same,&quot; making the incredibly rare, indestructible swords rather trite or rote when they do appear. The answer? Give them names and unique histories, and then, if this allows, expand on this with unique abilities. The same goes for Lunar spirit shapes. True, if you &quot;just&quot; have a fox or frog or whatever totem, then you'll not be penalized in any way, but it makes your character all the richer for having that extra description, of not only what that Lunar can do, but also themselves as a person. <br /> <br /> This may be my fondness for GSPs showing, though, as the idea of having a history for one of the component aspects of what makes your character, a bestial, mysterious shapeshifter godling, just seems to click, even if it never occurred for me prior to this conversation. In a way, its this narrative freedom that Exalted allows, that attracted me to the game in the first place; where a starting PC can radically alter the setting with some effort, as opposed to the movers and shakers all being crazy old man cosmic wizard lords who are also teenage girls (TM).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T01:28:12-08:00","id":46791,"title":"","content":"The article is in Danish, but the pictures are terrifying nonetheless. It is a huge goose barnacle which has appeared in Norway.<br /> <br /> That is a pretty terrifying spirit shape.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T13:01:38-08:00","id":47018,"title":"","content":"You want a cool memorable lunar spirit shape? Well here are some tips that might help:<br /> <br /> 1. DISCARD WOLVES, enough of wolf totems, think of something else unless you're not looking for something original or exotic.<br /> <br /> 2. If you already discarded wolves and haven't come out with a cool totem DISCARD MAMMALS, we humans are mammals and tend to think only on mammal terms, that is furry animals. Look for cool lizards, geckos, snakes (snakes are really cool), fishes (most of the vertebrate diversity is contained within fishes) and if you're looking for something beautiful/elegant, birds are for you. Remember that dinosaurs are elegible in Creation, build yourself a Triceraton full moon.<br /> <br /> 3. Still undecided... DISCARD VERTEBRATES, yeah, most people usually forget about the invertebrate coolness, even if the majority of animal diversity belongs to it (seriously vertebrates represent a small percentage of life on Earth). Look into some arthropod documentaries, look for sea slugs (many of them are beautiful and I'm not talking only about Glaucus atlanticus), echinoids (I have a starfish full moon), want something thar shines? ctenophora is for you, also, remember prehistoric invertebrates are also cool, ammonites, trilobites, sea scorpions, giant dragonflies, giant centipedes, etc. For the ultimate infinite shapes lunar go for the mighty sponge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://fivefoldcomicstance.thecomicseries.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Join the Strife</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/90-gonzo","name":"Gonzo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar90_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"934"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T13:23:08-08:00","id":47030,"title":"","content":"Random ones I have brainstormed/used:<br /> <br /> <b>Imperial Crane</b> - Full Moon bandit hero dude. Flashy and lots of bruvado, but cranes are actually kind of violent and physically strong, enduring and agile.<br /> <br /> <b>Wolverine</b> - First Age incarnation of a Lunar I made a while ago. About as expected. Strong, tough, good fighter.<br /> <br /> <b>Crocodile</b> - I had an elder Lunar in a game be the god of a local river. Lots of temples to him and he kind of kept local spirits in control. Forget what toem he was.<br /> <br /> <b>Bat</b> - Changing Moon insurgent, assassin and terrorist sort. Works for batman.<br /> <br /> <b>Ermine</b> - Kind of cliche classy, charismatic and slippery totem. Good for Changing Moons.<br /> <br /> <b>Hyena</b> - No Moon sorceress. Old Lunar in the Southeast who was a local source of many which legends and such.<br /> <br /> <b>Dhole</b> - Half Moon/No Moon. Great for thing slike tactical strategies and hunting in the dark of jungles. The cool head in her pack when I sat and brainstormed one up.<br /> <br /> And stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T13:47:10-08:00","id":47037,"title":"","content":"2e was a disaster for spirit shapes, because linking them to mutations -- while clever and well-intentioned -- meant that the way to get the most out of your shape was to reduce all potential shapes into &quot;what mutations can I get from this&quot;? Aside from leading to a disproportionate number of wacky Lunars, this took them in the opposite direction from the monsters they were intended to emulate. &quot;Monster people&quot; and &quot;beast people&quot; lean heavily on the animals with the most cultural purchase, which is to say that they skew heavily towards animals that resemble humans -- overwhelmingly they're fair-sized vertebrates who have a major role in human life, and the bulk are mammalian and cat-sized or larger. The problem with these animals is that they're the ones most likely to have &quot;superpowers&quot; that humans get for free, like being warm-blooded and intelligent, so they're poor mutation packages. I liked the way 2e Lunars handled spirit forms at first, but in retrospect, a system that discourages Lunar players from taking a wolf as their spirit shape is kind of fucked up.<br /> <br /> Ignoring all that, though, what animals <i>are</i> the most thematic and (to use the devs' term) mythically resonant? You can obviously look at actual mythology and popular metaphors here -- animals have always been a safe outlet for racial archetypes, e.g. the deceitful snake, the ferocious wolf, the stubborn goat. The academic term for this is &quot;zoosemy&quot; and if you search on that you can find more detailed studies of the practice as it relates to specific places, time periods, and animals. If you just want to build a &quot;top ten&quot; list without digging through world myths, look at popular culture, especially furries and animal otherkin, because the prevalence of animals in those areas reflects their dominance in the human psyche. Because there's such a strong and unbroken line of animal metaphor throughout history, I don't think our modern conceptions have changed all that much.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T15:10:45-08:00","id":47092,"title":"","content":"A lot of the time, it feels as if the books forget that Creation features animals that never were \u2013 fantastical beasts, but beasts nonetheless. Therefore...<br /> <br /> <b>Bangi Crawler/Bangi Fly</b><b>:</b> Any Caste, though I imagine it suits the Changing Moon and the No Moon best. Lots of poison, disguise and beauty, as well as oracular effects. Given the iconism of the creature's two stages of life, one might need to work out a way to have distinct two spirit shapes.<br /> <br /> <b>Ink Monkey:</b> I'm thinking Full Moon. An awful, sneaky, manipulative Full Moon who has mastered the outrageous lie and the bloody separation of bone and flesh.<br /> <br /> <b>Midwryth:</b> Probably most suited for a Changing Moon of the musical persuasion, probably with ties to Hell or the Guild; Black Claw Style is a given.<br /> <br /> <b>Snow Lion:</b> Perfect for the classic DBT ragebeast, but also a master of stealth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T18:38:46-08:00","id":47181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/35683-inspirations-for-lunar-spirit-shapes?p=47092#post47092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of the time, it feels as if the books forget that Creation features animals that never were \u2013 fantastical beasts, but beasts nonetheless. Therefore...<br /> <br /> <b>Bangi Crawler/Bangi Fly</b><b>:</b> Any Caste, though I imagine it suits the Changing Moon and the No Moon best. Lots of poison, disguise and beauty, as well as oracular effects. Given the iconism of the creature's two stages of life, one might need to work out a way to have distinct two spirit shapes.<br /> <br /> <b>Ink Monkey:</b> I'm thinking Full Moon. An awful, sneaky, manipulative Full Moon who has mastered the outrageous lie and the bloody separation of bone and flesh.<br /> <br /> <b>Midwryth:</b> Probably most suited for a Changing Moon of the musical persuasion, probably with ties to Hell or the Guild; Black Claw Style is a given.<br /> <br /> <b>Snow Lion:</b> Perfect for the classic DBT ragebeast, but also a master of stealth.</div> </div> </div> </div>Snow lions are not fantastical beasts, they're just extinct like the tyrant lizards and mammoths and things. I really enjoy the flavor of having these prehistoric animals in Creation. Anyone know (cause I don't) how well these things work for spirit shapes?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1658-maelstromseeker","name":"maelstromseeker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T21:19:03-08:00","id":47240,"title":"","content":"This one might be cheating, but an Electric Eel with more emphasis on the <i>Electric </i>part than that <i>Eel</i> part.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1252-god_of_awesome","name":"God_of_Awesome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1252_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-11T22:07:41-08:00","id":47254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/35683-inspirations-for-lunar-spirit-shapes?p=47092#post47092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of the time, it feels as if the books forget that Creation features animals that never were \u2013 fantastical beasts, but beasts nonetheless. Therefore...<br /> <br /> <b>Bangi Crawler/Bangi Fly</b><b>:</b> Any Caste, though I imagine it suits the Changing Moon and the No Moon best. Lots of poison, disguise and beauty, as well as oracular effects. Given the iconism of the creature's two stages of life, one might need to work out a way to have distinct two spirit shapes.<br /> <br /> <b>Ink Monkey:</b> I'm thinking Full Moon. An awful, sneaky, manipulative Full Moon who has mastered the outrageous lie and the bloody separation of bone and flesh.<br /> <br /> <b>Midwryth:</b> Probably most suited for a Changing Moon of the musical persuasion, probably with ties to Hell or the Guild; Black Claw Style is a given.<br /> <br /> <b>Snow Lion:</b> Perfect for the classic DBT ragebeast, but also a master of stealth.</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to be a Rapeape.....wait, I mean Rapace. Crazy ape are always fun at party, right ?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T11:41:24-08:00","id":47510,"title":"","content":"I like lists. Therefore, some of my favorite totems:<br /> <br /> 1. Tigers. Feline base-forms are pretty standard...but so COOL when you add stuff on. Winged tiger? Fire-breathing tiger with golden scales? Super-long serpentine tiger? Tiger with paralyzing venom? Chitinous Geiger-style Alien tiger? Giant city-stomping tiger? Tiger with poisoned quills it can fire at range? Ghost-tiger that walks through walls? Tiger is a great template to add neat stuff onto, and it always looks cool because tigers are really pretty. This is true of many of the generic spirits shapes. You can make 'em really awesome by building your own legend. A phantom tiger who walks silently through your walls and stands over your bed and drinks your breath as she kills you with nightmares about being hunted through the jungle is a completely different character than a tiger literally burning bright who drips molten metal and tears into Raksha armies with glowing iron claws...yeah. Tigers, awesome. About covered that, I guess. Lions are neat too, I guess?<br /> <br /> 2. Insects/Bugs/Small Arthropods/Invertebrates. Bombardier beetle Lunar saboteurs, Stag Beetle Full Moon seducers/seductresses with Twin-Faced Hero, Wasp-totem lunars with orderly armies of insect-children, cunning spider-totem planners, badass socialites with parasite totems, mantises who know Mantis, armor-plated poison-weilding scorpion warriors...whatever weird and freaky concept you wanna go with, there's a bug who is ALL ABOUT that one thing. Popular bugs often have mythic associations (biblical locusts, Anansi stories, Egyptian dung beetle myths, etc), but feel free to make up your own mythic stories and associations for your bug o' choice based on its real-world attributes. One of my recent favorite characters (a Nobilis character known as the Mosquito Queen, based on that legend about how all the animals wanted to team up and wipe humanity out but the mosquito talked them out of it) would make a great Lunar.<br /> <br /> 3. Frogs! Poisoned skin, super-jumps, sticky tongue-whip, sweet tree-climbin' abilities, can breathe underwater, known for singing songs of seduction and working at night, occasionally for eating things that look like they should be way too big for it to eat. Lots of mythic/magical associations, lots of neat powers, and different frogs offer a dazzling array of personality types: a Lunar based around a Golden Dart Frog totem might be a venom-packing socialite who struts his stuff like a peacock and just DARES his enemies to go after him, while a less flamboyant tree frog would make a great second-story man or stealthy thief/ninja type. Frog totem full moons might be aquatic ambush warriors or overly muscled terrors who leap hundreds of feet over their enemies and snatch them up into the air with a ridiculously long tongue. Frogs associate well with wisdom and shamanic imagery (they eat their own skin every day!), and you can probably stretch the &quot;I'm an amphibian&quot; far enough to justify supernatural regenerative powers to your ST even if frogs don't usually have those. They're a surprisingly good broad and adaptable sorta totem.<br /> <br /> 4. Giant Lumbering Sea-Beats: maybe it's just me, but I love whale and walrus and seal and shark-totem lunars. Their totem form is only really useful at sea, and I really like that limitation. It adds a sort of &quot;my place of power&quot; feel which I like. I like when Great White Shark Lunar is injured and on the run from the Wyld Hunt and can lure them out onto a ship to chase him and then just smile a super-toothy smile and say &quot;now it's my turn&quot; before taking advantage of his terrible ship-smashing super-mobile aquatic spirit shape. Sometimes it's really fun to try and lure your enemies into your arena, and to work with limits outside that arena. Sea-beasts are great for this because they're generally large and possessed of a great deal of stamina and symbolic staying power. Cultures all over the world have been making legends and myth out of sea-beasts forever, so themes are easy. Essentially, you get all the fun of being a Tyrant Lizard Godzilla, but it doesn't get boring because you don't turn into Tyrant Lizard Godzilla every session: you're only going into your terrifying Kaiju-form when the game takes the battle to the water. Also, at some point you're gonna get dropped out of an airship and turn into a whale to land on somebody and their army, because trust me, the rest of your Circle is trying to think of ways to abuse you for fun and profit.<br /> <br /> 5. Deep Sea Life: These are best for creepy characters, and I love me some creepy characters. Angler fish make great face-stealing social serial killers, giant squid and deep-water sharks make for interestingly flavored warriors or scholars, the Giant Marine Isopod is the most terrifying Deadly Beastman on the planet, and there's no character who isn't cooler if he can glow pretty colors to accentuate his coolness. I like Lunars as monsters and nightmares, and deep sea fish have huge eyes and giant teeth and alien forms. I want my lunar to distend his jaws and stomach to suddenly snap up and swallow a struggling enemy whole, or to use the themes of a deep-sea jellyfish dangling poisoned strands invisibly over large areas to ensnare anything that drifts into it (like spider-totem lunars only weirder). I love these especially for No Moons, because deep-sea shamans and sea-witches are some of my favorite ancient and dark magic images. You can go Lovecraftian here in a cool fey black-water-under-the-moon sorta way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T12:58:57-08:00","id":47568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/35683-inspirations-for-lunar-spirit-shapes?p=47510#post47510\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Also, at some point you're gonna get dropped out of an airship and turn into a whale to land on somebody and their army, because trust me, the rest of your Circle is trying to think of ways to abuse you for fun and profit.</div> </div> </div> </div>With access to even one bird-form, the airship is optional. My Full Moon concept refers to this as &quot;Enlightened Whale And Flowerpot Technique&quot;, because he was enlightened to the possibility by a flowerpot upside the noggin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I\u00e4! I\u00e4! Moe fthagn!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/280-valles","name":"Valles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar280_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"677"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-12T15:47:24-08:00","id":47658,"title":"","content":"Honestly, I find there are so many options for spirit shapes that my challenge is narrowing it down. Of course, I make a living studying animals, so I probably have a bit of a bias. Sources:<ul><li>Walker's Mammals of the World (2 Volumes) - usually you can find it in your local library</li> <li>Handbook of the Birds of the World (16 Volumes) - usually available in a good library...may need to hit your university.</li> <li>The Reptile Database (<a href=\"http://www.reptile-database.org/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.reptile-database.org/</a>) - for some reason, the reptile guys actually moved online early</li> <li>Amphibian Database (<a href=\"http://www.amnh.org/our-research/vertebrate-zoology/herpetology/amphibians-of-the-world-database\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.amnh.org/our-research/ver...world-database</a>) - few pictures, but cool details</li> <li>Fishes of the World - often in a good library...also in likely to need a university or big science section</li> </ul>I assume there are similar references for inverts, but I don't really do much with them. So that is the taxonomic side. The other way is to mine folktales, not just myth - there are some odd little references tucked away in folktales, including in some kids books.<br /> Anyway, hope those help!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/798-joshua","name":"Joshua","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar798_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-14T15:00:56-08:00","id":49310,"title":"","content":"Yikes...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.redbubble.com/people/nesling/works/15673780-loch-ness-monster-on-vacation?c=409846-mixed&amp;p=throw-pillow\" target=\"_blank\">Loch Ness monsters. On vacation. On a pillow.</a><br /> <br /> <br /> My wife is on <a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/artist/1Ngo336SKXWmoRnG3QWmhS\" target=\"_blank\">Spotify</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/864-jutlander","name":"Jutlander","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"467"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T00:11:40-08:00","id":49599,"title":"","content":"Doge-totem Lunar.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"http://i.imgur.com/YQjR1jo.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1878-adamantinerapier","name":"AdamantineRapier","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1878_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T00:41:16-08:00","id":49610,"title":"","content":"As I was reading through the books searching for a cool spirit shape for my new Lunar character, I was struck by the realization that the lines between human, animal, supernatural and &quot;other&quot; can get pretty damn blurry at times - which I like from a setting point of view but creates uncertainty when dealing with Lunars...<br /> <br /> Like, can your spirit shape be a Hushed One? I imagine it <i>can </i>be a demitaur, but what would a demitaur <i>warform </i>look like other than... a demitaur? Can your spirit shape be a furnace rhino, and would you get horns of magical materials? Could it be a mouse of the sun?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T07:19:19-08:00","id":49764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omicron</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/35683-inspirations-for-lunar-spirit-shapes?p=49610#post49610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I was reading through the books searching for a cool spirit shape for my new Lunar character, I was struck by the realization that the lines between human, animal, supernatural and &quot;other&quot; can get pretty damn blurry at times - which I like from a setting point of view but creates uncertainty when dealing with Lunars...<br /> <br /> Like, can your spirit shape be a Hushed One?</div> </div> </div> </div>Wyld-tainted human, out.on two counts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I imagine it <i>can </i>be a demitaur, but what would a demitaur <i>warform </i>look like other than... a demitaur? </div> </div> </div>Also Wyld-tainted, also out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can your spirit shape be a furnace rhino, and would you get horns of magical materials? Could it be a mouse of the sun? </div> </div> </div>Magical creature, so no. Natural weapons of a magical material require Charms to acquire, and the furnace rhino's processes reveal it to have superheated blood, which would be a touch too much of an advantage with regeneration. Just changing into one has the potential to break the setting, as the Lunar can just eat the appropriate raw material, day-in, day-out, and keep shedding horns via operation and healing Charms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T07:45:41-08:00","id":49780,"title":"","content":"I do wonder if Lunar will have charm that can modifying their totem in to mythological creature in 3rd, since unicorn-dolphin is obviously <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">M</span><span style=\"color:#00FFFF\">A</span><span style=\"color:#800080\">G</span><span style=\"color:#0000cd\">I</span><span style=\"color:#008000\">C</span><span style=\"color:#B22222\">A</span><span style=\"color:#4B0082\">L </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">right ?</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The no.1 fan of Demetheus. I also draw <a href=\"https://probably-unreliable.tumblr.com/tagged/Jenart\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted</a> things and is looking for commission works ~","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/298-jen","name":"Jen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar298_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T08:18:06-08:00","id":49813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/35683-inspirations-for-lunar-spirit-shapes?p=49780#post49780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do wonder if Lunar will have charm that can modifying their totem in to mythological creature in 3rd, since unicorn-dolphin is obviously <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">M</span><span style=\"color:#00FFFF\">A</span><span style=\"color:#800080\">G</span><span style=\"color:#0000cd\">I</span><span style=\"color:#008000\">C</span><span style=\"color:#B22222\">A</span><span style=\"color:#4B0082\">L </span><span style=\"color:#000000\">right ?</span></div> </div> </div> </div>The plan for EX3 chimerism is that it isn't stigmatized and represents changing the spirit shape by adding characteristics of another creature. That would cover a broad swath of mythological beasts. If there are any other options in chimerism, we haven't heard anything yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T08:37:43-08:00","id":49828,"title":"","content":"Unfortunately I can't say much here because I haven't played many Lunars, NPC or PC.<br /> <br /> That said, I did have a No Moon gunslinger with a nightengale totem. IIRC his Tell was having a nightengale's eyes, but I could be wrong.<br /> <br /> Also, I designed a Lunar whose totem was your typical wolf, but he did have a badass warform - how about a raging wolf-man made of swirling, molten moonsilver?<br /> <br /> Hmmm. Maybe I should start a topic on various warforms people have come up with...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/2480852/chapters/5503997\" target=\"_blank\">Glorious Echeladder Ascension Technique</a> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/287292-glorious-echeladder-ascension-technique-a-homestuck-exalted-crossover\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Topic</a><br /> <br /> &quot;Look, sometimes you just are in the mood to play the divinely empowered champion of the God of Farts. Mechanically optimized play is not the only way to enjoy playing your character.&quot; -Wise Old Guru","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1048-ryumaru","name":"Ryumaru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1048_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"326"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T10:16:38-08:00","id":49885,"title":"","content":"Probably my favorite character of all time was a Lunar with a Kangaroo spirit shape. He went around wearing moonsilver rollerblades (with actual blades on them). He was super athletic and had pretty much every speed/mobility charm he could get his hands on. His stunts were very reminiscent of Air Gear if anyone has watched/read it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1203-caladon","name":"Caladon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1203_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"142"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T11:19:44-08:00","id":49933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ryumaru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/35683-inspirations-for-lunar-spirit-shapes?p=49828#post49828\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unfortunately I can't say much here because I haven't played many Lunars, NPC or PC.<br /> <br /> That said, I did have a No Moon gunslinger with a nightengale totem. IIRC his Tell was having a nightengale's eyes, but I could be wrong.<br /> <br /> Also, I designed a Lunar whose totem was your typical wolf, but he did have a badass warform - how about a raging wolf-man made of swirling, molten moonsilver?<br /> <br /> Hmmm. Maybe I should start a topic on various warforms people have come up with...</div> </div> </div> </div>That's something I've considered for some time, especially with the Lunar I'm employing in Noodle's PbP game here; how to properly convey the idea of a &quot;Perfectly melding between human and totem forms&quot; of the warform without devolving to &quot; Upright animal with scary face&quot; or &quot; scary person with animal bits.&quot; The official art seems torn on this, too, with many going the former (Strength of Many, Tammuz, and of course, Ma-Ha-Suchi), while only a few go the other way (Anja Silverclaws, and to a lesser extent, Seven Devils Clever). While the former approach seems fine for those who wish to express their raw physical might, it doesn't gel well, at least to me, to those Lunars who get by on their looks, suavity, or wits. What amount of &quot;Animal&quot; traits is enough to convey the use of DBT, without making it just an excuse for catgirls?<br /> <br /> Actually, that's something of a roadblock I've had when I've tried to explain how cool Lunars are to newcomers to the game. They either see them as catgirl planeteers or furry vikings. The worst bit is I try to refute their claims, and then the Wardens of Gaia rear their heads, and I have to concede their points. Is it really that bad to play an urbane Lunar without being ostracized by many of your peers for not being &quot;HURR, CIVILIZATION WEAK, BARBARIAN STRONK?&quot;<br /> <br /> Finally, I've noticed a lot of love for insect totems here. If you're not familiar with it, Terra Formars may be something you'd be interested in looking into; a manga about astronaut soldiers spliced with bug genes fighting cockroach cavemen on Mars. Schlocky? Totally. Amusing as a battle comic? Incredibly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1586-dietaku","name":"Dietaku","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1586_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1095"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T11:27:28-08:00","id":49939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/35683-inspirations-for-lunar-spirit-shapes?p=49764#post49764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wyld-tainted human, out.on two counts.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Also Wyld-tainted, also out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't there a point at which &quot;Wyld-tainted&quot; is just an origin point for something that is integrated into Creation's ecosystem and breeds true without Wyld influence? I'm pretty sure the demitaurs, at least, are at that point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/85618-omicron-writes-stuff-hub-thread\" target=\"_blank\">Bits and pieces of Exalted setting.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/67-omicron","name":"Omicron","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar67_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1428"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T11:35:15-08:00","id":49944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dietaku</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/35683-inspirations-for-lunar-spirit-shapes?p=49933#post49933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While the former approach seems fine for those who wish to express their raw physical might, it doesn't gel well, at least to me, to those Lunars who get by on their looks, suavity, or wits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those Lunars shouldn't have DBT to begin with. Hybrid Body Rearrangement, <i>maybe</i>, but not DBT.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-01-15T11:40:39-08:00","id":49946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The MG</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/35683-inspirations-for-lunar-spirit-shapes?p=49944#post49944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those Lunars shouldn't have DBT to begin with. Hybrid Body Rearrangement, <i>maybe</i>, but not DBT.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being based on Werewolf strongly says otherwise. Though, of course, we're sitting on two past editions of poor execution.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}